9. Refunds and mandatory rights

After proper delivery, no additional voluntary change-of-mind refund is offered
unless stated in the order or required by the seller of record. A statutory
withdrawal right may be lost only where applicable law permits, after the
required separate express consent to immediate performance, acknowledgement of
that loss, contract confirmation and actual start of the relevant performance.
Receipt or activation of a key alone does not establish all these conditions.
For continuing services, the rules applicable to those services apply; issuance
of a key does not mean that all update services have been fully performed.

Nothing in this license excludes mandatory rights concerning non-delivery,
non-conformity, remedies, refunds, withdrawal or lawful payment disputes. The
applicable seller-of-record or store terms may grant additional rights. Earlier
purchases retain their agreed terms unless the purchaser validly agrees otherwise.
A valid refund may end only the paid entitlement refunded; it does not withdraw
the independent self-build permissions in section 2 or affect the user's data.
